  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Nigel Farage set for decisive but arguably empty victory in Clacton",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/aug/13/nigel-farage-set-for-decisive-but-arguably-empty-victory-in-clacton",
      "description": "<p>Leader of Reform UK on course to defeat Count Binface and an assortment of fringe candidates as polls close in Essex </p><p>Voting has closed in one of the UK’s more unusual and least tense byelections, with Nigel Farage set for a decisive if arguably empty victory against dozens of independent, fringe, extreme or otherwise oddball opponents.</p><p>The Reform UK leader <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/jul/07/nigel-farage-quits-as-mp-amid-scrunity-over-finances-clacton-reform\">sought re-election</a> to his Clacton seat in early July in an attempt to regain the political initiative following weeks of scrutiny over gifts he received and other aspects of his financial affairs.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/aug/13/nigel-farage-set-for-decisive-but-arguably-empty-victory-in-clacton\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-13T21:56:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "Polls close in Clacton byelection where Nigel Farage faces slew of fringe candidates",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/aug/13/clacton-byelection-polls-open",
      "description": "<p>Longest ballot in UK voting history features likes of Count Binface and Howling Laud Hope alongside Reform leader </p><p>Polls have closed in Clacton, where thousands of residents in the Essex seat voted in a ballot featuring Nigel Farage and a range of novelty and fringe candidates led by Count Binface.</p><p>The Reform UK leader resigned as the MP for Clacton at the start of July and forced a byelection in an attempt to address complaints over a deepening scandal about gifts he received.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/aug/13/clacton-byelection-polls-open\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-13T21:37:58"
    }
  ]
